  "body": "PR #942 (`Fixes #905`, merged as f490458a) judges an XY arc along its whole length against wall edges and corners in Boundary mode (`crates/sim/src/verify/arc_wall.rs`). Its high-tier review (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/942#pullrequestreview-5866783732) notes what is left: arcs in the XZ and YZ planes (G18 / G19) still get only the older joint reading (#839's union of chord joints), so a sharp corner between two joints of such an arc is still not measured.\n\nAlso from that review, smaller: no test covers the model-backed case of the new reading; the new suite `crates/app/tests/boundary_arc_walls.rs` uses only `verify` re-exports and belongs in `crates/sim/tests/` (#921's rule); the per-edge `Vec` allocation at `arc_wall.rs:135` could be avoided.\n\nPriority: P1, not P0 - XZ / YZ arcs project to straight lines in the XY wall plane, so the joint reading of the projected segment is much closer to exact than it was for XY arcs; confirm that argument with a test before relying on it, and raise to P0 if a gouge can pass.\n\nDone means: a test with a G18 and a G19 arc past a sharp wall corner between two joints either convicts or proves (with the numbers) that the projected reading cannot miss it; a model-backed pin exists; the suite sits in the sim crate.\n",
